    "html": "\n  <div class=\"hero-meta\">\n    <span class=\"level-badge\" data-level=\"3\">Level 3 - Intermediate</span><span class=\"time\">25 min</span>\n    <span class=\"chip warn\">Medium</span><span class=\"chip accent\">Linked list - merge sort</span>\n    <a class=\"chip\" href=\"https://leetcode.com/problems/sort-list/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">LC 148</a>\n  </div>\n  <h1>Sort List</h1>\n  <p class=\"lead\">Sorting a linked list in O(n log n) means merge sort: find the middle with slow/fast pointers, cut, sort both halves, and merge them by relinking nodes. No random access is needed, and the merge is O(1) extra space on a list. For the strict O(1)-memory follow-up, run the same merges bottom-up with run sizes 1, 2, 4, ...</p>\n"
